[Rendered](https://github.com/rust-lang/rfcs/blob/master/text/2920-inline-const.md)

TL; DR: Allows users to request compile-time evaluation without requiring promotion or a named `const`.

```rust
fn foo() -> &'static i32 {
    &const { 
        let x = 4i32;
        x.pow(5)
    }
}

fn main() {
    match *x {
        0 ..= const { u32::MAX / 2 } => println!("low"),
        const { u32::MAX / 2 + 1 } ..= u32::MAX => println!("high"),
    }
}
```

This idea has been in the ether for a while now as a way to [reduce dependence on promotion](https://github.com/rust-lang/rust/pull/70042#issuecomment-612221597) for evaluating simple expressions at compile-time. It was discussed most recently on [Zulip](https://rust-lang.zulipchat.com/#narrow/stream/213817-t-lang/topic/.22Why.20use.20.60const.60.20over.20.60let.60.3F.22).

Credit to @scottmcm, who discussed this with me on Zulip and was one of the people who [discovered this idea](https://internals.rust-lang.org/t/quick-thought-const-blocks/7803). I believe both @RalfJung and @oli-obk have considered this as well.

This RFC provides Rust with the possibility to partially pattern-match lambda’s arguments with the `..` syntax:

```rust
// x.map expects a function taking five i32 and returning a i32
x.map(|_, _, _, _, _| 0);
x.map(|..| 0);
x.map(|a, _, b, ..| a + b);
```

[Rendered](https://github.com/phaazon/rfcs/blob/rfc/partial-lambda-args/text/0000-partial-closure-args.md).

This RFC introduces the `$self` macro metavariable, a companion to `$crate`, that allows macros hygienic access to items. With `$self`, a macro `m` could be declared as:

```rust
mod submod {
    static PRIVATE: &'static str = "PRIVATE_SUBMOD";

    #[macro_export]
    macro_rules! m {
        () => (println!("{}", $self::PRIVATE))
    }

    pub use m;
}

pub fn main() {
    submod::m!(); // `PRIVATE` unconditionally resolves to `submod::PRIVATE`
}
```

On expansion of `m`, `PRIVATE` unconditionally resolves as if it were at the definition site, that is, to `submod::PRIVATE`.

[Rendered](https://github.com/SergioBenitez/rfcs/blob/self-metavar/text/0000-self-macro-metavar.md)
